  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1154 PM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nThe upper-level pattern will remain unsettled for the second half\nof this week, as a series of upper level troughs and embedded\ndisturbances swing through the area through the end of the week.\nHowever, models continue to keep conditions drier across the area,\nresulting in little to no precipitation chances through Friday. A\nslightly stronger upper-level trough is expected to track north \nof the area over the weekend, bringing some increased chances for\nlight showers across parts of West Central Texas mainly on\nSaturday. A larger/more potent upper-level ridge is expected to\nbuild across the area for the early part of next week. As for \ntemperatures, Generally a cooler and drier air mass will remain \nacross the area with no really cold air on the way. Overnight low\ntemperatures in the 40s and 50s are expected through the long term\nforecast, with afternoon high temperatures expected to , and then\n40s. Highs mainly in the 70s for Wednesday and Thursday, cooling\ninto the 60s for Friday through Sunday, and gradually climbing\nback into the 70s for the first half of next week.",
